         lint {:doc "Run clj-kondo linter; fails on warnings (usage: bb lint)"
               ;; The ratchet is closed: the tree is at 0 warnings and 0 errors, so
               ;; --fail-level warning now enforces that. A new warning fails the
               ;; build rather than joining a backlog (#33).
               ;;
               ;; If this starts failing on something that is genuinely a false
               ;; positive rather than debt, add a NARROW exclusion to
               ;; server/.clj-kondo/config.edn with the reason — every entry there
               ;; has one. Do not widen the level back out; the whole value of the
               ;; gate is that the count cannot drift upward silently.
               ;;
               ;; Two things worth knowing before acting on a warning here.
               ;; Warnings on .cljc files are frequently platform-split false
               ;; positives: a require or var declared unconditionally and used only
               ;; inside #?(:clj ...) reads as unused to the :cljs pass, and deleting
               ;; it breaks the build while lint still reports 0 errors — bb test is
               ;; what catches that, not this task. And fixing one warning can raise
               ;; the count: wrapping a defn in a reader conditional can orphan the
               ;; last cljs-visible use of one of its requires, which then reads as
               ;; unused on that pass. There is a worked example with the reasoning
               ;; written next to it at server/src/digdir/data/db.cljc:1183-1196 —
               ;; wrapping create-folder alone would have gone 1 warning to 2,
               ;; because it was the only cljs-visible user of nano-id; the fix was
               ;; to move that require under #?(:clj ...) as well.
               ;;
               ;; src-dev is linted too. It was omitted originally, which meant the
               ;; enrichment skills, the demo skill graphs and the dev tools were
               ;; never checked — and a genuine "Unresolved var" (a call to a
               ;; config-db fn deleted by the dataset rename) sat there unnoticed
               ;; while the gate reported 0 errors.
               :task (clojure {:dir "server"} "-M:clj-kondo" "--lint" "src" "src-dev" "test" "--fail-level" "warning")}

